{"name":"Pickled Radish","hex":"#ee1144","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pickled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of pickle"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Preserved by pickling.","Drunk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pickled"},{"term":"radish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the Brassicaceae family, Raphanus sativus or Raphanus raphanistrum subsp. sativus, having an edible root.","The root of this plant used as food. Some varieties are pungent and usually eaten raw in salads, etc., while others have a milder taste and are cooked."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pickled radish","blocks":[{"text":"Pickled radish, called chikin-mu in Korean, is a radish dish served and eaten with Korean fried chicken. Like other banchan, it is a free side dish in South Korea."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pickled_radish","wikidata":"Q28802529"},{"title":"Pickling","blocks":[{"text":"Pickling is the process of preserving or extending the shelf life of food by either anaerobic fermentation in brine or immersion in vinegar. The pickling procedure typically affects the food's texture and flavor. The resulting food is called a pickle, or, if named, the name is prefaced with the word \"pickled\". Foods that are pickled include vegetables, fruits, mushrooms, meats, fish, dairy and eggs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Gherkins_and_Onions.JPG/330px-Gherkins_and_Onions.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pickling","wikidata":"Q1503967"},{"title":"Radish","blocks":[{"text":"The radish is a flowering plant in the mustard family, Brassicaceae. Its large taproot is commonly used as a root vegetable, although the entire plant is edible and its leaves are sometimes used as a leaf vegetable. Domesticated in Asia, radishes are grown and consumed globally. The radish is sometimes considered to form a species complex with the wild radish and instead treated as the subspecies Raphanus raphanistrum subsp. sativus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Radish_3371103037_4ab07db0bf_o.jpg/330px-Radish_3371103037_4ab07db0bf_o.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radish","wikidata":"Q7224565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg/500px-Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg/500px-Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Torshi, traditional pickles in Southeast Europe, West Asia and Northern Africa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG/1280px-PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kosher torshi in Israel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wiki